514	    /// Regression test: an undotted prerelease suffix such as `alpha1` (common in
515	    /// packages migrated from other toolchains) must have its numeric suffix
516	    /// carried forward rather than reset to 0.  Before the fix, the only prefix
517	    /// pattern tested was the dotted form `"{tag}."`, so `strip_prefix("alpha.")`
518	    /// on `"alpha1"` returned `None`, the counter stayed at 0, and the output was
519	    /// `1.2.3-alpha.0` — meaning consecutive bumps would silently lose the
520	    /// existing sequence number.
521	    ///
522	    /// Note on SemVer ordering: `"alpha"` < `"alpha1"` lexicographically (the
523	    /// dotted identifier `alpha` is a strict ASCII prefix of `alpha1`), so
524	    /// `1.2.3-alpha.2 < 1.2.3-alpha1` per spec.  The invariant we can assert is
525	    /// that the counter increments from the existing numeric suffix (not from 0),
526	    /// so future same-format bumps remain monotonically increasing.
527	    #[test]
528	    fn bump_prerelease_from_undotted_tag_produces_higher_version() {
529	        // Use base="1.2.2" + Patch so that bump(base, Patch)="1.2.3", matching
